      "description": "Controlling refreshed prose: research/plan-machine-learning-track.md, complete pair section and Current published supplier reconciliation (SHA-256 348a19b0017653faf85a3708273ef33461a42a3d1dffb0e3861684b7f53fff73). Read its complete current contract and referenced prerequisite modules; preserved historical wording does not override the dated interface repair. This is prose planning, not proof acceptance.\n\n**Pages:** ml02-linear-classification / ml02-linear-classification-examples. **Scope:** Define binary and multiclass linear-score classifiers with an explicit deterministic label tie rule; indicator-response least-squares classification; LDA with class-conditional $N(\\mu_k,\\Sigma)$ densities, common positive-definite covariance, and positive class priors; QDA with positive-definite class-specific covariances; binary logistic $P(Y=1\\mid x)=\\{1+\\exp[-(\\beta_0+x^T\\beta)]\\}^{-1}$ and multiclass softmax linear-logit models; L1-penalized likelihood $-\\ell(\\beta)+\\lambda\\|\\beta\\|_1$ with an explicitly excluded intercept when desired; and the perceptron. Expanding Gaussian log densities gives affine LDA log-posterior scores only under the common covariance premise, while QDA scores are quadratic. Logistic regression is conditional and assumes no Gaussian feature law. With augmented design $X$ (including the intercept), state $\\ell(\\beta)=\\sum_i[y_i x_i^T\\beta-\\log(1+e^{x_i^T\\beta})]$, whose Hessian is $-X^TWX$ for $W_{ii}=p_i(1-p_i)$. When $X$ has full column rank and the current coefficients are finite, $W\\succ0$; the exact Newton/IRLS step is $z=X\\beta+W^{-1}(y-p)$ and $\\beta_{new}=(X^TWX)^{-1}X^TWz$. This algebra does not promise iterative convergence. Under complete separation, the unpenalized likelihood supremum need not be attained at a finite coefficient. Define perceptron updates on augmented inputs $\\tilde x_i=(x_i,1)$: in a fixed cyclic order, update $w\\leftarrow w+y_i\\tilde x_i$ whenever $y_iw^T\\tilde x_i\\le0$. If a finite sample has a unit separator with margin $\\gamma>0$ and $\\|\\tilde x_i\\|\\le R$, prove termination after at most $R^2/\\gamma^2$ mistakes; no convergence is asserted for nonseparable data, where cycles can occur.\n\n**Proof route:** Derive the LDA/QDA scores by density expansion; derive logistic gradient and Hessian and solve the weighted least-squares Newton equation under full rank. For perceptron, include the complete progress/norm-squared mistake-bound proof, not the source’s exercise as evidence. State separation and nonattainment by an explicit diverging coefficient sequence. Avoid coefficient-equivalence claims between LDA and logistic outside separately stated model/estimation conditions.\n\n**Examples:** Generative LDA and conditional logistic boundaries; a separated sample with diverging logistic coefficients; a nonseparable perceptron cycle.\n\n**Requires:** published `thm-hessian-characterises-convexity`, `thm-least-squares-solutions-and-normal-equation`, and `thm-singular-value-decomposition`, with their finite-dimensional hypotheses. Logistic MLE existence and asymptotic confidence remain separate results. **Sources:** [ESL] Chapter 4 §§4.1–4.5, printed pp. 101–135, especially perceptron update (4.44) and Exercise 4.6; §18.4, pp. 661–664. Exercise 4.6 is not treated as a completed proof.",
