        {
          "id": "def-indicator-response-least-squares-classifier",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Indicator-response least-squares classification",
          "deps": [
            "def-linear-score-classifier"
          ],
          "statement": "Let $n,q\\ge1$ and $K\\ge2$ be finite integers. For a fixed design matrix $X\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times q}$ and labels $y_i\\in\\{1,\\ldots,K\\}$, form the indicator response matrix $Y\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times K}$ by $Y_{ik}=1$ when $y_i=k$ and $Y_{ik}=0$ otherwise. For a coefficient matrix $B\\in\\mathbb R^{q\\times K}$, set $L(B)=(2n)^{-1}\\|Y-XB\\|_F^2$, where $\\|A\\|_F^2$ is the sum of squares of all entries of $A$. Let $B_*$ be the least-squares minimizer with smallest Frobenius norm. For a new row vector $x^T\\in\\mathbb R^{1\\times q}$, the indicator-response classifier assigns scores $(x^TB_*)_k$ and predicts the smallest class index attaining their maximum. An intercept, if used, is one of the columns of $X$; no rank assumption is imposed on $X$.",
          "strategy": "Define the one-hot response matrix, squared-error objective, and deterministic minimum-Frobenius-norm fit; its existence is discharged by the local lemma.",
          "sources": {
