          "title": "A disconnected graph on concentric circles separates the rings",
          "statement": "Let $V=\\{1,\\ldots,8\\}$ and, for $j\\in\\{0,1,2,3\\}$, set $x_{j+1}=(\\cos(\\pi j/2),\\sin(\\pi j/2))$ and $x_{j+5}=3(\\cos(\\pi j/2),\\sin(\\pi j/2))$. Build a graph with unit-weight edges $\\{1,2\\},\\{2,3\\},\\{3,4\\},\\{4,1\\}$ and $\\{5,6\\},\\{6,7\\},\\{7,8\\},\\{8,5\\}$, and no other edges. Deterministic unnormalized spectral clustering with $k=2$ and no row normalization returns the two concentric rings as its clusters. This finite graph example makes no statement about manifold recovery for other graph constructions.",
