ion to absolute precision ε on the bounded-conditioning/amplitude families specified below costs O((N+L)log(N+L)log(1/ε)). Do not extend these costs to full training or infer long-context accuracy. Proposed items: def-recurrent-neural-network; def-lstm-cell; def-linear-state-space-model; def-s4-dplr-parameterization; alg-s4-state-space-recurrence-and-convolution; thm-hippo-leg-matrices-have-low-rank-structure; thm-dplr-discretized-step-linear-cost; lem-roots-of-unity-fft-complexity; thm-s4-convolution-filter-complexity. **Proof route:** unroll recurrence to identify convolution kernel. Conjugate NPLR matrices to DPLR; Woodbury gives bilinear discretization and recurrence; for the parallel filter evaluate truncated generating function on roots of unity, use the matrix resolvent and Woodbury to reduce to diagonal-plus-low-rank Cauchy products, then apply the Cauchy algorithm. Prove the roots-of-unity DFT orthogonality and radix-2 FFT cost locally, together with the Woodbury/Cauchy multiply bounds; state invertibility of I−ΔA/2 and the low-rank Woodbury correction in the bilinear update; no inspected library FFT theorem supplies these steps. **Examples:** LSTM gate equations; same SSM evaluated recurrently or by convolution; finite-precision Cauchy cost caveat. **Requires:** matrix multiplication/Woodbury algebra and finite roots-of-unity identities, with the FFT complexity proof included locally. No upstream neural result. Backpropagation-through-time and vanishing/exploding-gradient analysis are outside this architecture claim. **Sources:** Goodfellow, Deep Learning, Chapter 10 §§10.1–10.5 and 10.8–10.10.1; Gu et al., “Efficiently Modeling Long Sequences with Structured State Spaces,” §§2.1–2.4, 3.1–3.3 and Appendix C.1–C.3. Long-range-dependency motivation and benchmarks are contextual/empirical.\n\n**2026-10-19 numerical proof qualification:** The local lem-cauchy-root-grid-matvec-numerical-cost supplies a constructive near/far arc-tree proof on a separated scaled 