al infeasible/reversed-quantifier lower statement; give the strengthened exact construction, padding, small-diameter and KL/Pinsker argument locally. This is not discounted-return RL, and the theorem does not extend to uncommunicating/transient-state models without changes. Proposed interfaces: def-communicating-mdp-and-diameter, def-average-reward-and-regret, alg-ucrl2, thm-ucrl2-high-probability-regret, thm-ucrl2-regret-lower-bound. **Proof route:** establish reward and categorical-$L^1$ confidence events, span-of-bias $\\le D$, extended-value-iteration approximation, failed-confidence episode bounds, and the doubling-count sum; derive the lower bound from the source's hard-MDP construction. **Examples:** noncommunicating model, large diameter, discounted/average-reward target mismatch. **Requires:** ML-72 — Finite MDPs and Bellman operators; def-time-homogeneous-markov-chain-with-transition-kernel, def-filtration-and-filtered-probability-space, def-martingale-difference-sequence, def-martingale-submartingale-and-supermartingale, lem-conditional-hoeffding-bound-for-bounded-martingale-differences, and thm-azuma-hoeffding-inequality; carry the Axiom of Choice required by the Markov-chain supplier. **Sources:** Jaksch–Ortner–Auer, *Near-optimal Regret Bounds for Reinforcement Learning*, complete JMLR PDF pp. 1–38 (printed pp. 1563–1600): model/diameter and Theorem 2, pp. 2–5; UCRL2 and confidence/episode construction, pp. 7–12; regret proof, pp. 12–21; Theorem 5 and hard-instance proof, pp. 22–27. The theorem's probability and initial-state quantifiers are retained.",
