bservations, and exponential policy-tree growth. **Requires:** ML-72 — Finite MDPs and Bellman operators; def-measure-kernel-and-probability-kernel, thm-measurability-of-integration-against-a-kernel, def-conditional-probability-given-a-sigma-algebra, and thm-bayes-formula-for-dominated-kernels, specialized to the finite sets and positive observation normalizer. **Sources:** Kaelbling–Littman–Cassandra, Brown CS-96-08, full PDF pp. 1–29; mathematical body pp. 3–27 (PDF p. 2 blank): belief update and belief-MDP reduction, PDF pp. 9–11; policy trees and linear belief value, pp. 12–16; finite-horizon piecewise-linear convex value and witness pruning, pp. 16–19. The text layer loses mathematical symbols, so equations were checked in the cached PDF.",
      "items": [
