          "dependency_level": 2,
          "statement": "Input a finite POMDP, a horizon $H\\in\\mathbb N$, and its discount $\\gamma\\in[0,1]$. A depth-zero policy tree is the empty continuation and has the zero vector $\\alpha_0:S\\to\\mathbb R$. Recursively, a depth-$(h+1)$ policy tree consists of a root action $a\\in A$ and one depth-$h$ continuation tree for each observation $o\\in\\Omega$. If the continuation vectors are $(\\alpha_o)_{o\\in\\Omega}$, assign the tree the vector\n\n$$\\alpha_{a,(\\alpha_o)}(s)=r(s,a)+\\gamma\\sum_{s'\\in S}T(s'\\mid s,a)\\sum_{o\\in\\Omega}O(o\\mid s')\\alpha_o(s')\\qquad(s\\in S).$$\n\nSet $\\Gamma_0=\\{\\alpha_0\\}$. For each $h=0,\\ldots,H-1$, form $\\Gamma_{h+1}$ from every action $a\\in A$ and every tuple $(\\alpha_o)_{o\\in\\Omega}\\in\\Gamma_h^{\\Omega}$ using the displayed formula, treating $\\Gamma_{h+1}$ as a set so equal vectors are stored once. Return $(\\Gamma_0,\\ldots,\\Gamma_H)$. This procedure exhaustively enumerates finite policy-tree vectors; it does not perform linear-program witness pruning and makes no bit-complexity or polynomial-time claim.",
          "strategy": "Enumerate all finite observation-contingent policy trees by root action and one continuation tree per observation, and compute their state-conditional values recursively.",
