          "dependency_level": 3,
          "statement": "Let a finite POMDP be fixed, let $b\\in\\Delta(S)$ and $a\\in A$, and put $\\bar b(s')=\\sum_{s\\in S}T(s'\\mid s,a)b(s)$, $q(o)=\\sum_{s'\\in S}O(o\\mid s')\\bar b(s')$, and, when $q(o)>0$, $\\tau(o)(s')=O(o\\mid s')\\bar b(s')/q(o)$. For Borel $C\\subseteq\\Delta(S)$ define $K(C)=\\sum_{o:q(o)>0}q(o)1_C(\\tau(o))$. Then the joint next-state/reward/observation mass in the POMDP definition is normalized; $\\bar b$ and $q$ are probability distributions; every defined $\\tau(o)$ is a probability distribution and is the conditional law of the next state given observation $o$; and $K$ is a probability measure. Moreover, $(b,a)\\mapsto K(C\\mid b,a)$ is Borel measurable for each Borel $C$, so $K$ is a probability kernel from $\\Delta(S)\\times A$ to $\\Delta(S)$. No Axiom of Choice is used.",
