          "dependency_level": 4,
          "statement": "Let $S=\\{s_0,s_1\\}$, $A=\\{a\\}$, $\\Omega=\\{x,y\\}$, reward alphabet $\\{0\\}$, and horizon $H=1$ with $\\gamma=1$. For each $i\\in\\{0,1\\}$, the joint next-state/reward law assigns probability one to $(s_i,0)$ from $(s_i,a)$, so the hidden state remains fixed and the reward is zero. Let $b_0(s_0)=3/4$, $b_0(s_1)=1/4$, and set $O(x\\mid s_0)=3/4$, $O(x\\mid s_1)=1/4$, $O(y\\mid s_0)=1/4$, and $O(y\\mid s_1)=3/4$. The probability of observing $x$ is $5/8$, and after $x$ the belief is $b_1(s_0)=9/10$, $b_1(s_1)=1/10$.",
