          "statement": "Let $S=\\{s_0,s_1\\}$, $A=\\{a\\}$, $\\Omega=\\{x\\}$, reward alphabet $\\{0\\}$, horizon $H=1$, and discount $\\gamma=1$. From each state, the joint next-state/reward law assigns probability one to the same state with reward zero. Let $b_0(s_0)=2/3$, $b_0(s_1)=1/3$, and let $O(x\\mid s_0)=O(x\\mid s_1)=1$. Then $q(x\\mid b_0,a)=1$ and the posterior after $x$ is again $(2/3,1/3)$; the observation does not distinguish the two hidden states.",
