        {
          "id": "lem-real-cholesky-recurrence-computes-factorization",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "The real Cholesky recurrence computes the positive-diagonal factor",
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$ and let $M\\in\\mathbb R^{n\\times n}$ be symmetric positive definite, meaning $x^TMx>0$ for every nonzero $x\\in\\mathbb R^n$. Initialize $R$ as the zero $n\\times n$ matrix. For $j=1,\\ldots,n$ in order, set\n$$p_j=M_{jj}-\\sum_{k<j}R_{jk}^2,\\qquad R_{jj}=\\sqrt{p_j},$$\nand then, for $i=j+1,\\ldots,n$ in order, set\n$$R_{ij}=\\frac{M_{ij}-\\sum_{k<j}R_{ik}R_{jk}}{R_{jj}}.$$\nEvery pivot $p_j$ is positive, so the recurrence is well-defined and returns a lower-triangular matrix $R$ with positive diagonal satisfying $M=RR^T$.",
          "deps": [
            "def-cholesky-factorisation-with-positive-diagonal",
